"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.1372399312845963,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.116969995,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":78.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"CeriBell, Inc. operates as a medical technology company in the United States. It develops the Ceribell System, a novel and point-of-care EEG platform specifically designed to address the unmet needs of patients in the acute care setting. The company also offers disposable, flexible headbands, and headcaps; and a pocket-sized, rechargeable battery-operated recorder used to capture and wirelessly transmit EEG signals; and Clarity, an AI-powered seizure detection algorithm. In addition, it operates an EEG portal, which enables real-time remote access to a patient's EEG data. The company was formerly known as Brain Stethoscope, Inc. and changed its name to CeriBell, Inc. in August 2015. CeriBell, Inc. was incorporated in 2014 and is headquartered in Sunnyvale, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Xingjuan  Chao Ph.D. | Co-Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 327 people. Revenue per employee of $272K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $37K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["CeriBell, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.0B market cap on $89M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +36% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Gross margins of 87% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The company is burning through $42M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -30.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 14% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 66% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.13002364066193764},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 179% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfort